.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Advanced Disk Catalog plugin

@Contents
$ #Advanced Disk Catalog plugin#
   ~Browsing ADC databases~@ADCBrowse@

   ~ADC plugin configuration~@ADCCfg@

   ~Registering ADC plugin~@ADCReg@

@ADCBrowse
$ #Browsing ADC databases#
    Using the ADC viewer you can browse contents of your
ADC databases. Unregistered users of ADC can browse only first
five disks due to ADC format limitations. Howewer, if yoy are
registered user of ADC and wish to view your databases from
another computer (for example via network), you will be able to
do it if you have option 'Create IDX files' checked on computer
with registered ADC version and .idx files already exist.
This plugin have full support for categories. You can view them
in full (LCtrl-3) mode.

 Use <Ctrl-A> to toggle 'archives as folders' option while
 viewing catalog

 Use <Alt-F3>/<Alt-F4>/<F4> to display detailed information
 about current item including full comments in standart
 FAR viewer/editor window

@ADCCfg
$ #ADC plugin configuration#
    In this dialog you can alter following options:

 #Free memory#                 If this option is active, then
                             memory allocated for directory structure
                             would be released immediately, not on
                             plugin shutdown. It greatly speeds up
                             search/shutdown process

 #Treat archives as folders#   Enables treating archives as
                             ordinary folders

 #Create IDX files#            Enable creating IDX files thus
                             reducing time needed for opening
                             databases and allowing to view large
                             databases from another computer

 #Startup mode#                Sets startup mode for plugin
                             0 - no mode change, 1-9 - set
                             corresponding mode (just like LCtrl 1-9)

 #Thousands sep#               Specifies character that used when
                             separating number fields in info/view
                             panels. Leave this field blank if you
                             do not want to separate them at all.

@ADCReg
$ #Registering ADC viewer plugin#
You can read registartion issues in readme.txt file, supplied
with this plugin

     When you register ADC plugin you will get following features:
       1. Ability to create index files for fast or remote
          access to your databases
       2. Full 'archives as folders' support (Shareware version
          displays only first 10 archives as folders)

Russian citizens can get full version of ADC viewer for free.
